# kui-ejs — Cline / Continue.dev rules
# Canonical source: AGENTS.md

## Discover before generating

Fetch the AI-facing catalog:
- `GET /api/registry?index=1` — full catalog (no source) — ~5x smaller
- `GET /api/registry` — full catalog with inline EJS source per partial + variants
- `GET /llms-full.txt` — markdown dump
- Offline fallback: `public/registry/components.json`
- Per-partial markdown chunks: `public/components/<id>.md`

Filter `components[]` by `layer` (`ui` | `app` | `domain` | `theme`), `category`, `name`, or `filePath`. Follow `composes[]` recursively when porting a partial; `usedBy[]` is the inverse.

## ⚠️ Catalog sync — REQUIRED

**Any time you add, rename, or remove a partial (`modules/ui/`, `modules/app/`, `modules/domain/<vertical>/`), a theme (`views/theme/<vertical>/` + `src/routes/themes/<vertical>.ts`), a data file (`src/data/<vertical>.data.ts`), or a `showcase.menu.ts` entry, run:**

```bash
npm run registry:snapshot
```

**before committing.** This regenerates `public/registry/components.json` + `public/registry/components.index.json` + `public/components/*.md` from the showcase data. The same script runs automatically via the `prebuild` npm hook before `npm run build`, but you must still commit the regenerated files so the catalog stays in lockstep with the code. A stale catalog misleads every AI agent that reads it — treat it as broken-build severity.

## Hard rules

1. Server-rendered Express + EJS only — no React/Vue/htmx/Alpine/SPA bundling.
2. `<%= value %>` for user data (escaped). `<%- html %>` only for trusted EJS / pre-built HTML; document in `docs/raw-output-allowlist.md`.
3. `<%- include('partials/foo', locals) %>` for partial includes.
4. Token-only styling: `bg-primary`, `text-text-secondary`, `border-border-focus`. No raw hex.
5. Font Awesome via CDN only. `<i class="fa-solid fa-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>`.
6. Accessibility: `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons, `aria-label` on icon-only buttons, semantic HTML, `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-border-focus`.
7. Sample data in `src/data/<vertical>.data.ts`. Static data only.
8. No business logic in views — keep them presentational.

## Where new code goes

- `modules/ui/` — primitive + composed EJS partials
- `modules/app/` — shells, navigation, drawers, state placeholders
- `modules/domain/<vertical>/` — industry-specific partials
- `views/theme/<vertical>/` — multi-page demos
- `src/routes/themes/<vertical>.ts` — Express router per theme
- New theme → also register in `src/routes/themes.ts` and `src/data/showcase.menu.ts`
